[218.458097, "o", "\u001b[38;5;208m● belay\u001b[0m\r\n  Before I lock this in — quick summary, then one question.\r\n\r\n  **Does July change anything?** Mostly confirms the original draft, with one correction:\r\n\r\n  | category | onboarding draft (Apr–Jun) | naive May–Jul avg | **using now** |\r\n  |---|---|---|---|\r\n  | groceries | 297.97 | 306.15 | **306.15** ✓ refreshed |\r\n  | dining_out | 25.85 | 37.96 | **37.96** ✓ refreshed |\r\n  | subscriptions | 25.74 | 25.78 | **25.78** ✓ refreshed |\r\n  | car | 72.56 | 214.12 | **72.56** ⚠ kept, see below |\r\n\r\n  July's actuals landed right on baseline (groceries, dining, subscriptions), so those three get bumped up to the fresher May–Jul average. **Car is the one that would've gone sideways**: July's car spend was €505.04, but €420 of that is the annual insurance payment your CLAUDE.md already flags as a July-only yearly-bank item — it's not a car-cost trend, it's a once-a-year lump handled separately. Averaging it into a rolling window would've tripled the August car target (€214.12) for money that isn't due again until next July. I held car at €72.56 (Apr–Jun, insurance-free) instead — July's fuel-only spend (€85.04) confirms that's still the right range.\r\n\r\n  No yearly-bank item is due in August, income stays at €2,800 (confirmed again by July), so **savings_target comes out to €2,357.55**.\r\n\r\n  One question: **anything unusual planned for August** — trip, event, one-off purchase — that should get its own line before I lock the draft in?\r\n\r\n\u001b[1;36malex ▸ \u001b[0m"]
